From: ddf2@cornell.edu (David Friedman)
Subject: GUNS: Don't buy Chinese

>>I would like to discourage people on this list from buying guns, or any other 
>>products, made in mainland China.  As we remember from the student uprisings
>>in 
>>Beijing, China has one of the most repressive governments on earth.  
>
>I would strongly second Simon's appeal, and (not surprisingly to those who
>know me) cite as well China's exceptionally inhumane treatment of the
>people of Tibet. (Left)

I disagree. China has an oppressive government, and that may be an argument
against buying Chinese goods, but China does not have "one of the most
oppressive governments on earth." There are a number of African countries,
Burundi for example, which, judged by the government's treatment of its own
population, are very  much worse. There are other Asian countries--Burma
comes immediately to mind--which are at least as oppressive.

So far as the original point about not buying goods, the problem is that if
you refuse to buy Chinese goods because they may be made by government
slaves, or because you want to protest the massacre of students, you are
also refusing to buy the goods of capitalist entrepreneurs who are doing
their best to replace a communist system with a capitalist one. My guess is
that a much larger fraction of the goods China exports are in the second
category, capitalism being a generally much more productive system than
socialism.

